  statement: For every CNF φ with m clauses and n variables, the minimal local induction dimension of the noncommutative algebra generated by φ is at most O(n^(2/3) * m^(1/3)).
  rationale: The local induction dimension of a noncommutative algebra can capture the complexity inherent in the structure of an CNF's clauses. This could potentially expose hidden structures in circuits that are not easily captured by standard circuit measures, providing new insights into circuit monotone width.
